# Trivy ignore list for the CI tooling image.
#
# Scope: this file applies to the build-time tooling image only. That image is
# never shipped, never reaches a user device, and never serves traffic. The
# dependencies that reach production are gated separately and independently by
# `npm run security:audit:prod`, which runs with --omit=dev and currently
# reports 0 critical and 0 high.
#
# Every entry carries an expiry. When it lapses, Trivy reports the finding again
# and the gate goes red until someone re-evaluates. Entries are not permitted
# without a reason and an expiry.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Go standard library, compiled into the esbuild binary
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Package:       node_modules/@esbuild/linux-x64/bin/esbuild
# Owner:         release-engineering
# Reason:        esbuild is a transitive devDependency of vitest via vite 6.4.3,
#                which declares esbuild ^0.25.0. 0.25.12 is already the newest
#                release in that range, so the Go stdlib cannot be advanced
#                without a vite major upgrade. Forcing an out-of-range override
#                risks breaking the build toolchain to patch a binary that never
#                ships.
# Exploitability: Build-time only. esbuild runs inside an ephemeral, non-root,
#                read-only, network-isolated CI container, over this
#                repository's own first-party source. These stdlib CVEs require
#                processing untrusted input, which does not occur here.
# Re-evaluate:   when vite is upgraded to a release accepting esbuild >= 0.26.
CVE-2025-61726 exp:2026-12-01
